WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:10.711
[Kaspar]: You are listening to Clap to Collap on Collaboradio.org

2
00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:40.637
[Kaspar]: as a part of Freie Radio's Berlin Brandenburg, streaming on fr-bb.org and collaboradio.org, transmitting on DAB Plus channel 7D in Berlin and channel 12D in Brandenburg.

3
00:00:42.139 --> 00:00:59.187
[Kaspar]: In this radio show, sound artist Kasper König presents interviews and sound recordings from Colab, Technobiological Futures, a project by the artist-run Bio and Hacking Labs, hosted on Hectoria.org and sponsored by Prohevitia.

4
00:01:00.388 --> 00:01:12.131
[Kaspar]: Listeners are invited into a global network of makers, exploring the collective motivations behind the work and the unique context of this collaborative lab culture.

5
00:01:12.131 --> 00:01:21.673
[Kaspar]: The show is edited and produced between Zurich and the Emmental, so expect a few holes here and there, both in the sound and the narrative.

6
00:01:23.054 --> 00:01:31.579
[Kaspar]: Alongside uncovering these collaborations, the episode dips into music and sound art made in the Daivo spirit.

7
00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:33.461
[Kaspar]: Do it with others.

8
00:01:33.461 --> 00:01:42.006
[Kaspar]: Kasper König himself, a sound artist, also shares his fascination with unexpected sounds and surprising discoveries from the workshop.

9
00:01:42.006 --> 00:01:42.427
[Kaspar]: Enjoy!

10
00:02:03.789 --> 00:02:05.050
[Kaspar]: So how are you?

11
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:13.777
[Kaspar]: I just wanted to chat some small talk and then we deep dive into these three questions that I prepared or that you maybe saw already.

12
00:02:14.745 --> 00:02:24.910
[Kaspar]: I'm curious to know also a bit more how you're doing just around the project and not just only the project wise.

13
00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:31.814
